    "created_at": "2018-09-12T01:42:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-12T01:42:41Z",
    "body": "I don't think you need to specify anything in particular about margins since [CSS Align](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-align-3/#self-alignment) already specifies how it works. If anything, you could say that the `<legend>`'s margin-box is used (or more generally, that the fieldset/legend alignment uses the block-level rules). So, author auto-margins should just work.\r\n\r\nBTW, [here's my original arguments](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1488228#c23) for why `justify-self` is the ideal property to use for this. I'm even more convinced now that this is the way to go because mapping it to some auto-margin value is [pretty complicated](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1488228#c19) when the fieldset/legend have different `writing-mode`. It's not something that you can express using CSS rules.\r\n\r\n@zcorpan can you update the spec to use `justify-self` please?  I think it's better if people review that proposal rather than auto-margins.",
